Now that you know how `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` is structured, it's time to edit it and regenerate the color assets the app actually reads.

## Edit a Token

Open `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` and change one or more tokens under `colors`, `borderRadius`, or `typography`. For example, update the primary brand color for both light and dark mode, and increase the medium border radius:

```json
{
  "themes": {
    "vonage": {
      "colors": {
        "light": { "primary": "#1D6FE6" },
        "dark":  { "primary": "#5FA0FF" }
      },
      "borderRadius": {
        "medium": 10
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Save the file once you've made your edit.

## Regenerate `SemanticColors.xcassets`

From the `VERA/` directory, run the theme generator script:

```sh
python3 ./Scripts/generate-app-theme.py
```

The script reads `Theme/semantics.json` and (re)generates the `VERACommonUI/VERACommonUI/Resources/SemanticColors.xcassets` asset catalog, writing one `.colorset` per semantic token with both its light and dark values. On success, you'll see:

```
✅ Generated 14 semantic colors in SemanticColors.xcassets
```

| Script | Run from | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `generate-app-theme.py` | `VERA/` | `Theme/semantics.json` | `VERACommonUI/VERACommonUI/Resources/SemanticColors.xcassets` |

{% aside type="caution" %}
If `semantics.json` has invalid JSON (a trailing comma, a missing quote, etc.), the generator script fails with something like:

```
❌ Error parsing JSON: Expecting ',' delimiter: line 8 column 5 (char 172)
```

Fix the JSON syntax in `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` and re-run `python3 ./Scripts/generate-app-theme.py` from `VERA/`.
{% /aside %}

Next, you'll confirm your generated output without building or running the app.

This Codespace doesn't have Xcode or macOS available, so you can't build, run, or open the iOS app to see your changes visually. Instead, "verification" in this tutorial means confirming that each Generator_Script printed a success message and that the generated files it wrote actually contain the values you edited.

